<title>USA: Chicago real estate firm wins $17.5 mln GSA deal.</title>
<headline>Chicago real estate firm wins $17.5 mln GSA deal.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Equis Corp, a privately held Chicago-based real estate firm, said Thursday it has won three contracts from the U.S. General Services Administration valued at $17.5 million.</p>
<p>The company said the contract calls for it to provide leasing, administration and acquisition services for federal government offices and facilities in the South, Central and West regions of the country.</p>
